'''Maroniko''' ({{lit|[[Maroon Confederacy|maroon]] speech}}; {{Langx|kz|ߡߊߙߐߣߌߞߏ|Màròníkò}}), also known as '''Araucarian''' (''arakawiano''; {{Langx|kz|ߊߙߊߞߊ߲|Árákán}}) outside of [[Balisca]], is a [[W:Creole language|creole language]] that emerged in the [[Maroon Confederacy]] (what is now the community of [[Araucaria]]) as a result of the mixing of [[W:Yoruba language|Imo]], [[Ajami]] and the [[Kurupiran languages]] amongst [[Maroon Wars|self-liberated]] [[W:Maroons|maroons]]. Later migration led to the emergence of the Maroniko-speaking [[Sanyan Creoles|Creole community]] in [[Sanyan]].

